      "rationale": "RetroDECK links the core's own texture directory into one shared tree. The answer names the directory the emulator opens and the directory the bytes are really in, exactly as a save placement does — and the option file switches replacement on, so 'enabled' is a live read.",
      "input": {
        "home": "/home/deck",
        "files": {
          "/home/deck/.var/app/net.retrodeck.retrodeck/config/retrodeck/retrodeck.json": "{\"paths\": {\"rd_home_path\": \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck\", \"saves_path\": \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck/saves\", \"bios_path\": \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck/bios\"}, \"version\": \"0.10.9b\"}",
          "/home/deck/.var/app/net.retrodeck.retrodeck/config/retroarch/retroarch.cfg": "libretro_directory = \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck/cores\"\nsystem_directory = \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck/bios\"\nsavefile_directory = \"/mnt/sd/retrodeck/saves\"\n",
          "/home/deck/.var/app/net.retrodeck.retrodeck/config/retroarch/retroarch-core-options.cfg": "reicast_custom_textures = \"enabled\"\n",
          "/mnt/sd/retrodeck/texture_packs/retroarch-core/Flycast/textures/readme.txt": "put packs here"
